From: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:53:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] x86/pci: Prefer ECAM over type 1 configuration access

raw_pci_read() and raw_pci_write() use configuration type 1 for domain 0
and registers below 256 whenever it is available, and ECAM only above
that. Under a hypervisor, type 1 costs two exits per access: the write
of the address to 0xcf8 and the access at 0xcfc. On QEMU's q35 the
0xcf8 write cannot be coalesced either, as the ICH9 reset control
register at 0xcf9 splits the coalesced range, so each one is an exit to
userspace; a boot of a guest with a handful of virtio devices makes
about 1,500 of them. ECAM costs one exit per access.

Use ECAM first once MMCONFIG is set up. Until then raw_pci_ext_ops is
NULL and type 1 is used, as before.

On an x86_64 KVM guest (q35, one vCPU) this takes 4.5 ms off the time
from kernel start to "Freeing unused kernel image" (p50 of 20 boots,
interleaved): acpi_init() goes from 18 to 14 ms and the virtio-pci
probe from 5.5 to 4.2 ms.

The trade-off: on real hardware type 1 is preferred for registers below
256 because some platforms' MMCONFIG is unreliable; this is only safe
where the ECAM region is known to cover every bus, as in a VM.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/x86/pci/common.c | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/pci/common.c b/arch/x86/pci/common.c
index 63105b29f..0f08239f8 100644
--- a/arch/x86/pci/common.c
+++ b/arch/x86/pci/common.c
@@ -40,20 +40,28 @@ const struct pci_raw_ops *__read_mostly raw_pci_ext_ops;
 int raw_pci_read(unsigned int domain, unsigned int bus, unsigned int devfn,
 						int reg, int len, u32 *val)
 {
-	if (domain == 0 && reg < 256 && raw_pci_ops)
-		return raw_pci_ops->read(domain, bus, devfn, reg, len, val);
+	/*
+	 * Prefer ECAM once MMCONFIG is set up: under a hypervisor a type 1
+	 * access is two exits, the address written to 0xcf8 and the access at
+	 * 0xcfc, where an ECAM access is one. This is only correct where the
+	 * ECAM region covers every bus, as it does on QEMU's q35. Until then
+	 * raw_pci_ext_ops is NULL and type 1 is used.
+	 */
 	if (raw_pci_ext_ops)
 		return raw_pci_ext_ops->read(domain, bus, devfn, reg, len, val);
+	if (domain == 0 && reg < 256 && raw_pci_ops)
+		return raw_pci_ops->read(domain, bus, devfn, reg, len, val);
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
 int raw_pci_write(unsigned int domain, unsigned int bus, unsigned int devfn,
 						int reg, int len, u32 val)
 {
-	if (domain == 0 && reg < 256 && raw_pci_ops)
-		return raw_pci_ops->write(domain, bus, devfn, reg, len, val);
+	/* See raw_pci_read(). */
 	if (raw_pci_ext_ops)
 		return raw_pci_ext_ops->write(domain, bus, devfn, reg, len, val);
+	if (domain == 0 && reg < 256 && raw_pci_ops)
+		return raw_pci_ops->write(domain, bus, devfn, reg, len, val);
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
